      "start_seconds": 1.16,
      "end_seconds": 5.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "uh, sorry, doctor, shall I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.62,
      "end_seconds": 10.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "okay yes have a seat. Tell me what's going on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.07,
      "end_seconds": 21.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.36,
      "text": "Yeah uh it's a swollen red eyelid. I don't know what's causing it. Sorry I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.95,
      "end_seconds": 25.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.69,
      "end_seconds": 35.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.31,
      "end_seconds": 60.08,
      "duration_seconds": 9.77,
      "text": "okay: respiratory rate 18 pressure 115 over 75 saturation 96 percent pulse 88. When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.52,
      "end_seconds": 64.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "It's been going on for ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.37,
      "end_seconds": 74.55,
      "duration_seconds": 9.18,
      "text": "hm, okay. Can you describe it it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.17,
      "end_seconds": 88.72,
      "duration_seconds": 13.55,
      "text": "I'd say all the time. A six out of ten, I suppose. And there's a fever as well, three days now. There's double vision as well"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.18,
      "end_seconds": 93.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.23,
      "end_seconds": 96.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Mild, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.91,
      "end_seconds": 100.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "a few quick ones: recent injury or sinus infection?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.7,
      "end_seconds": 107.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "no recent injury or sinus infection, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.61,
      "end_seconds": 112.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.88,
      "end_seconds": 114.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "no rashes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.69,
      "end_seconds": 137.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.16,
      "end_seconds": 143.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "I I take carvedilol 6.25 milligrams twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.03,
      "end_seconds": 148.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.12,
      "end_seconds": 156.5,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "I have heart failure it's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.03,
      "end_seconds": 164.1,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "yes heart failure is known to us good to have that clear. Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.06,
      "end_seconds": 172.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "I had a cataract operation in my left eye about a year ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.06,
      "end_seconds": 189.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.37,
      "end_seconds": 193.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Yes diclofenac it gives me wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.58,
      "end_seconds": 197.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "do you work outside the the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.22,
      "end_seconds": 203.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.54,
      "end_seconds": 211.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "How active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.87,
      "end_seconds": 215.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.46,
      "end_seconds": 218.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.41,
      "end_seconds": 221.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.55,
      "end_seconds": 226.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.46,
      "end_seconds": 236.45,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "sure thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.11,
      "end_seconds": 241.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "right, stay as you are for a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.41,
      "end_seconds": 257.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "the eyelid is swollen shut, the eye is bulging and the movements are painful and limited"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.41,
      "end_seconds": 277.12,
      "duration_seconds": 17.71,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Okay, thinking it through, it fits best with orbital cellulitis. It could also be periorbital cellulitis, so we'll keep that open. I'd like to arrange an urgent CT scan for orbital cellulitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.52,
      "end_seconds": 282.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Erm, where would I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.96,
      "end_seconds": 304.56,
      "duration_seconds": 21.6,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood tests for orbital cellulitis. You need admission today for intravenous antibiotics. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Come back straight away. Alright, that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.35,
      "end_seconds": 308.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Hmm no that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}